ith option credit\"; base DCF alone is $200. I will use:\n   CENTRAL IV = $210 (50%/80% CI in Section 4).\n   Note: NO DCF-only conclusion; multiples cross-check: guided FY26 GAAP EPS\n   $8.79 mid \u00d7 18x = $158; \u00d7 22x = $193; \u00d7 25x = $220; \u00d7 27x \u2248 $237. Current 38.9x\n   guided EPS requires a perfect compounder multiple with litigation tail-risk.\n   Multiples confirm the DCF; they do not rescue the price.\n\nSECTION 3.5 \u2014 SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n3.5-1 Competitive response: Qualcomm/Nokia/Ericsson cross-license and monetize\n   similar SEP portfolios; if IDCC's streaming model succeeds, implementers\n   (Disney, Netflix, Apple) may coordinate FRAND-defense (Disney's suit, DOJ\n   interest). Impact on model: \u22122 (downside).\n3.5-2 Reflexivity: high stock price \u2192 SBC attracts engineers (the company's only\n   real input), and litigation credibility rises. Low price \u2192 talent flight and\n   licensee stalling. NET: +1.5 positive reflexivity.\n3.5-3 Customer evolution: early adopters (Amazon) \u2192 mainstream (Disney, others).\n   LTV per deal rising (streaming bundles devices+services), but per-deal CAC\n   (litigation cost) also rising. Watch: litigation expense run-rate \u2014 Q2 opex +27%\n   YoY. [Actual in pack: SG&A $68M FY25 vs $63M FY24]\n\nSECTION 4 \u2014 SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nPrior: base rate 45% chance of ARR target delivery.\nLikelihood update from evidence: ARR +13%, Amazon agreement, Disney UPC injunctions,\nguidance raise, DOJ statement favorable \u2192 posterior 60% on base delivery.\n\nScenario probabilities (sum