ion flag).\nCrowding risk score: 10/15 (momentum + sell-side + short base = high two-sided\ncrowding). Position cap \u22121pp.\n\nSECTION 6 \u2014 PORTFOLIO FIT\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nIDCC is a \"legal-beta\" asset: high correlation to risk appetite (beta ~1.4\nvendor-rated), long-duration, and net-cash. In a portfolio context:\n   Positive: negative correlation to AI-hardware/physical-capex cycle; acts as\n   an IP-royalty diversifier, 97% gross margin, no refinancing risk.\n   Negative: common bear trigger with other growth longs is rising REAL RATES\n   (duration compression); IDCC's 1.41 beta amplifies the drawdown.\nFit: OK as a 2\u20133% satellite, NOT as a core holding. At current price, fit = 0%.\n\nSECTION 6.5 \u2014 KELLY SIZING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nPayoff structure (per $1 invested at $342):\n   Bear 25%: $125 \u2192 \u221263%\n   Base 50%: $200 \u2192 \u221242%\n   Bull 25%: $300 \u2192 \u221212%\n   Expected return = 0.25\u00d7(\u22120.63) + 0.50\u00d7(\u22120.42) + 0.25\u00d7(\u22120.12) = \u22120.40 (i.e., \u221240%\n   expected total return over the 3\u20135yr horizon; roughly \u221210%/yr).\n   Edge = negative \u2192 Kelly fraction = 0%. Fractional Kelly (25%) = 0%.\n   RECONCILIATION WITH LAYER 5: Layer 5 scores the THESIS (company quality), not\n   the INVESTMENT. Gap between Layer 5 sizing (4\u20136%) and Kelly (0%) exceeds 20pp \u2192\n   RE-ANALYSIS TRIGGER. Resolution: valuation dominates; the thesis is good but the\n   price is wrong. FINAL SIZE = 0% new money.\n\nSECTION 7 \u2014 RISKS & CATALYSTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nCatalysts (next 12 months):\n   1) Amazon arbitration outcome (final video RAND rate) [Unconfirmed timing]\n   2) Disney litigation: motion-to-dismiss decision; DOJ brief already favorable\n   3) Q3'26 convert settlement ($80.3M principal; zero net dilution due to hedges)\n   4) New streaming/CE/IoT license signings (count per quarter)\n   5) Q3/Q4 2026 results vs. raised guidance ($775\u2013845M)\n   6) 6G standardization milestones (2027-28)\nRisks:\n   1) Antitrust adverse ruling on SEP licensing model (Disney case)\n   2) Arbitration sets video royalty below expectations \u2192 Streaming ARR cap ~$150M\n   3) Catch-up revenue exhaustion: TTM FCF includes >$100M one-offs\n   4) Warrant/conversion dilution: 6.0M warrants at $105.43 mature net-share\n      2027-2028 \u2192 ~4.2M shares (16% of basic) \u2014 [Actual, company release]\n   5) SG&A/enforcement cost inflation (Q2 opex +27% YoY)\n\nSECTION 7.5 \u2014 CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nCommon bear trigger with portfolio: real-rate spike (10Y >5%) \u2014 impacts IDCC\n(duration) + all long-duration growth holdings simultaneously.\nTail correlation: in 2022-style stress, high-beta high-multiple names converge.\nCVaR (5% tail): IDCC drawdown 40\u201350% \u2192 $170\u2013205 within 6 months if a Disney\nruling or arbitration disappointment coincides with a rates spike. At $342,\nCVaR per share \u2248 \u2212$150.\nPortfolio-level: cap IDCC at 0% (new money); existing holders cap 3%.\n\nSECTION 8 \u2014 MONITORING RULES\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nThesis KPIs (from Tornado + Section 7):\n   1) ARR growth: must stay \u226510% YoY. If <5% for 2