s a mild positive; high real rates pressure long-duration multi-year licensing cash streams mildly negative. Net \u2248 neutral.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n## SECTION 1.5. BASE RATE & HISTORICAL PATTERN\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 1.5-1. Base Rate Inquiry**\n| Question | Base Rate | Applied |\n|---|---|---|\n| 5-year survival for established high-margin licensor | >85% | Yes |\n| Company hitting a 4.5-year growth target ($1B ARR) | ~40\u201360% | 50% in base |\n| Platform transition (patents \u2192 streaming/cloud licensing) succeeds | ~20\u201330% | Bull case; partially |\n| Large-value licensing arbitration outcome favors licensor | ~50\u201360% | Neutral |\n| Regulatory/antitrust changes force licensing-rate compression | ~20\u201335% | Bear case |\n\n**Step 1.5-2. Deviation from Base Rate \u2014 Justification**\n- My base-case probability of hitting the $1B ARR target (~50%) is near the base rate, not above it.\n- Company-specific mitigants: (1) existing Amazon streaming/cloud agreement signed, (2) two UPC injunctions won against Disney across 11 EU countries, (3) record smartphone ARR, (4) 6 new licenses in Q1 2026. These raise confidence modestly but do not justify >1.5x base rate.\n\n**Step 1.5-3. Base Rate Shock Check:** No red flag triggered. Market is implicitly pricing ~90\u2013100% achievement probability, above the 2.0x base-rate red flag threshold \u2014 **this flags the market's optimism, not my model.**\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n## SECTION 2. BUSINESS QUALITY\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 2-1. Business Understanding**\nInterDigital invents wireless (3G/4G/5G/6G), video codec, and AI technologies; contributes them to global standards bodies; and licenses the resulting patents to device makers and streaming/cloud services. It monetizes an R&D \"patent tollbooth\" \u2014 near-zero marginal cost per unit licensed, with revenue in the form of recurring ARR plus lumpy catch-up payments. Understandability: **HIGH.**\n\n**Step 2-2. Moat Score (0\u20133 each; total /21)**\n\n| Moat Type | Score | Direction |\n|---|---|---|\n| Intangible assets (patents, standards leadership) | 3 | Widening (6G, AI, video) |\n| Switching costs | 2 | Stable (SEP/Frand framework) |\n| Network effects | 1 | Stable |\n| Cost advantage | 1 | Stable |\n| Economies of scale | 2 | Widening (R&D spread over growing base) |\n| Regulatory barriers | 2 | Narrowing (DOJ antitrust attention) |\n| Data moat | 1 | Widening (3GPP leadership) |\n| **Total** | **12/21** | **Wide Moat; Stable-to-Widening** |\n\n**Step 2-3. Lynch Classification: FAST GROWER** (ARR +13% YoY, EPS +65% in 2025). Checkpoints: sustainable growth runway (phone install base + streaming + IoT + auto + 6G), manageable incremental costs (60%+ EBITDA margins), balance sheet strong.\n\n**Step 2-4. Financial Strength Scorecard [Actual - filed]**\n- Revenue 3-yr CAGR (FY22\u2013FY25): **22.1%** (458\u2192834M)\n- TTM revenue: $788M; FY26E guidance $775\u2013845M [Company guidance]\n- Operating margin FY25: **55.3%** (TTM); 12-yr median: 40.5%\n- Net margin FY25: **48.8%**; ROE: 26.4% (vendor)\n- FCF margin FY25: **63.4%** (pack FCF basis; 529/834)\n- Net debt/EBITDA: **Net cash \u2248 $720M** [Estimate \u2014 $1.1B cash+ST inv [Company Q2'26] less $380M converts [Company]]\n- Interest coverage: N/A (net cash)\n- **Overall: EXCELLENT**\n\n**Step 2-5. Capital Allocation Scorecard (0\u20133 each)**\n1. **Buyback efficiency: 2** \u2014 $23M in Q2'26 at ~$230\u2013$340 range; reasonable not aggressive\n2. **M&A track record: 2** \u2014 Mostly organic R&D; no major impairments\n3. **Capex efficiency: 3** \u2014 $16M capex (filings) on $529M FCF; vendor-basis ~$65\u201371M still trivial\n4. **Rationality of mix: 3** \u2014 Dividend ($18M/qtr) + buybacks + heavy R&D\n5. **Guidance accuracy: 3** \u2014 Q2'26 revenue $260M vs guided $139\u2013143M; raised FY26 by $85M\n- **Total: 13/15.** Insider holding 1.58% \u2014 no bonus/penalty.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n## SECTION 2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 2.5-1. R&D Capitalization (approximation)**\n- R&D expense \u2248 $200M/yr [Estimate \u2014 implied from opex and SBC structure]\n- Capitalize over 4 years \u2192 unamortized R&D asset \u2248 $500\u2013600M [Assumption]\n- Adjusted Operating Income \u2248 $461M (FY25) + $200M \u2212 $150M amortization \u2248 **$511M** [Estimate]\n- Adjusted NOPAT \u2248 $511M \u00d7 (1\u221218%) \u2248 **$419M** [Estimate]\n- Adjusted Invested Capital \u2248 Equity $1.101B + debt $0.380B \u2212 cash $0.739B + unamortized R&D $0.55B \u2248 **$1.29B** [Estimate]\n- **Adjusted ROIC \u2248 32%** vs GAAP ROIC ~36% on a smaller base \u2014 still an exceptional franchise.\n\n**Step 2.5-2. SBC Treatment**\n- FY25 SBC: $43M [Actual \u2014 filed]\n- Owner FCF = Reported FCF $529M \u2212 SBC $43M \u2248 **$486M** (FY25) [Estimate]\n- Normalized owner FCF (ex-catch-up timing) \u2248 **$330\u2013370M** [Assumption]\n\n**Step 2.5-3. Leases:** Negligible (<$20M operating leases) [Actual].\n**Step 2.5-6. Owner Earnings FY25:** NI $407M + D&A $78M \u2212 maintenance capex (est.) $25M \u2212 \u0394WC $20M \u2212 SBC $43M \u2248 **$397M** [Estimate].\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n## SECTION 3. VALUATION \u2014 ENGINE 1 (DCF + Multiples)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n### Discount Rate Derivation\n- Rf: **4.70%** [Actual \u2014 10Y Treasury, Aug 2026]\n- ERP: **4.50%** [Assumption \u2014 Damodaran-style mature-market ERP]\n- Beta: **1.10** [Assumption \u2014 fundamental beta for a net-cash licensing business; vendor CAPM beta is 1.41 but window/benchmark is unknown and equity beta likely overstates fundamental risk]\n- **Cost of Equity (Ke) = 4.70 + 1.10 \u00d7 4.50 = 9.65%** [Assumption]\n- Debt: negligible (net cash) \u2192 **WACC \u2248 9.65%**\n\n### Explicit Forecast (Base Case)\n\n| Year | Revenue ($M) | EBITDA ($M) | Margin | D&A | EBIT | Cash Tax (18%) | Capex* | \u0394WC | SBC | Int. Inc. | FCFE |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026E | 810 | 499 | 61.6% | 80 | 419 | 75 | 65 | 20 | 50 | 33 | **327** |\n| 2027E | 885 | 531 | 60% | 80 | 451 | 81 | 65 | 20 | 55 | 40 | **350** |\n| 2028E | 965 | 560 | 58% | 80 | 480 | 86 | 70 | 20 | 60 | 35 | **359** |\n| 2029E | 1,050 | 578 | 55% | 85 | 493 | 89 | 75 | 20 | 60 | 30 | **364** |\n| 2030E | 1,150 | 600 | 52% | 85 | 515 | 93 | 80 | 25 | 65 | 25 | **362** |\n| 2031E | 1,220 | 622 | 51% | 90 | 532 | 96 | 85 | 25 | 70 | 20 | **366** |\n\n*Capex uses the broader definition including capitalized software/patent procurement (~$60\u201370M/yr), not the filed $16M PPE-only number. Sources: 2026 revenue/EBITDA from company guidance [Actual \u2014 company]. 2027\u20132031 growth path anchored to company's $1B ARR / $600M EBITDA 2030 target [Actual \u2014 company] with catch-up revenue stabilizing at $120\u2013150M and margin compressing toward 52% [Assumption]. Capex, WC, SBC, tax, and interest assumptions are my own [Assumption]. Explicit forecast beyond 2031 is not established by company guidance; I extend only 3% growth into terminal [Assumption].\n\n### Terminal Value\n- Terminal FCF growth: **2.5%** [Assumption \u2014 \u2264 long-run nominal GDP]\n- TV2031 = 366 \u00d7 1.025 / (0.0965 \u2212 0.025) = **$5,245M** [Arithmetic]\n\n### DCF Summary\n| Component | PV ($M) |\n|---|---|\n| 2026E FCFe | 298 |\n| 2027E FCFe | 319 |\n| 2028E FCFe | 299 |\n| 2029E FCFe | 276 |\n| 2030E FCFe | 250 |\n| 2031E FCFe | 231 |\n| PV of Terminal Value | 3,309 |\n| **Enterprise Value** | **$4,982M** |\n| Add: Net cash (cash + ST inv $1,100M \u2212 debt $380M) | $720M |\n| Add: PV of warrant proceeds (6.0M \u00d7 $105.43, ~2027\u201328) | ~$570M [Estimate] |\n| **Equity Value** | **$6,272M** |\n| Pro-forma fully diluted shares | 33.4M [Estimate] |\n| **Base Fair Value / share** | **\u2248$188** [Estimate] |\n\n### Sensitivity \u2014 Discount Rate \u00d7 Terminal Growth\n\n| Ke \\ g | 2.0% | 2.5% | 3.0% |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 8.5% | $232 | $245 | $260 |\n| 9.65% | $178 | $188 | $200 |\n| 11.0% | $135 | $141 | $148 |\n\n### Reverse DCF\nTo justify $342/share, the market requires: **base-year FCF \u2248 $470M (2025-level, without SBC haircut) growing 8% for 10 years**, at a 9.65% discount rate. Equivalently, a 2030 FCF of ~$620M (not $400M) discounted at <8.5%. The current price bakes in near-total success of the 2030 plan.\n\n### Comparable Multiples\n- Trailing P/E: 40.5 (vendor) vs quality-compounder range 20\u201328\n- 2026E P/E (non-GAAP $11.83 guidance mid): **28.9\u00d7**\n- EV/2026E EBITDA: $8.12B \u00f7 $499M = **16.3\u00d7**\n- The 16.3x forward EBITDA multiple is *reasonable for a 13% ARR grower*, but the EBITDA quality is diluted by catch-up revenue, which is non-recurring.\n\n**Multiples alone neither confirm nor refute fair value \u2014 but they show the price leaves no room for execution misses.**\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n## SECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 3.5-1. Competitive Response:** If IDCC succeeds in streaming licensing (Amazon, Disney), expect Nokia, Ericsson, and Qualcomm to push their own video/streaming patent pools. MPEG LA and HEVC Advance patent pools are direct competitors. Counter-move severity: **\u22123** (price competition in licensing rates).\n\n**Step 3.5-2. Reflexivity:** Stock at $342 strengthens IDCC as litigation counterparty (perceived financial durability, ability to fund multi-jurisdiction enforcement). A sharp drop would embolden licensees to delay deals. Positive reflexivity is currently in play.\n\n**Step 3.5-3. Customer Behavior:** Early adopter streaming licensees (Amazon) set the template; mainstream (Disney, Netflix, Apple TV+) will wait for arbitration/Frand benchmarks. LTV/CAC likely stable; churn risk emerges only if a court rules against Frand licensing terms.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n## SECTION 4. SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Prior (Base Rate):** ~50% chance of meeting $1B ARR/2030 target.\n**Bayesian updates from current evidence:** +5 pts (Amazon contract \u2192 streaming program validated), +5 pts (UPC injunctions vs. Disney), \u22125 pts (DOJ antitrust involvement), \u22125 pts (revenue volatility; Q1/Q2 2026 down YoY). **Posterior base-case probability: ~50\u201355%.** [Estimate]\n\n| Scenario | Prob. | Key Drivers | 2030 EBITDA | Fair Value |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Bear** | 35% | DOJ action caps rates; Amazon arbitration disappoints; Disney wins on appeal; ARR only $820M; margin 50% | $450M | **$135** |\n| **Base** | 45% | ARR ~$1.0B; $600M EBITDA target achieved; streaming scales; catch-up normalizes at ~$120M | $600M | **$188** |\n| **Bull** | 20% | Streaming acceleration + IoT/auto + 6G pull forward; ARR $1.2B; margins hold 58% | $750M | **$330** |\n\n**Expected Value = 0.35\u00d7$135 + 0.45\u00d7$188 + 0.20\u00d7$330 = $198** [Arithmetic]\n\n**50% CI: $150 \u2013 $260; 80% CI: $130 \u2013 $330** [Estimate]\n**Margin of Safety at $342: (198\u2212342)/198 = \u221273% (Base case: \u221282%) \u2014 NO SAFETY MARGIN.**\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n## SECTION 4.5. TIME HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2