ies re-acceleration fears unresolved.\n\n1-2 Regime probability distribution (must sum 100%):\n   \u2022 Reflation (high rates + growth): 35%\n   \u2022 Stagflation (high rates + low growth): 30%\n   \u2022 Recession (low rates + low growth): 20%\n   \u2022 Goldilocks (low rates + growth): 15%\n   The 10Y at 4.74% precludes a low-rate Goldilocks base case.\n\n1-3 IDCC macro sensitivity (each \u22123 to +3):\n   Rate sensitivity: \u22122 (long-duration royalty stream; high multiple compresses)\n   Dollar sensitivity: +1 (royalties billed in USD to global OEMs)\n   Liquidity sensitivity: +1 (contract/legal cycles are credit-independent)\n   Economic-cycle sensitivity: +0.5 (handset/CE volumes)\n   Commodity sensitivity: 0\n\n1-4 Macro alignment: Regime-weighted expected impact = slightly negative\n   (Recession + Stagflation = 50% combined). NEUTRAL-TO-HEADWIND.\n   Conviction \u22120.5. No change to intrinsic value; affects entry timing only.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 1.5 \u2014 BASE RATE CHECK\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n1.5-1 Similar-enterprise base rates:\n   \u2022 Patent-licensing firm 5-yr survival: ~90%+ (IP persists through litigation).\n   \u2022 ARR target delivery (management-stated $1B by 2030 from $626M = 10.5% CAGR):\n     base rate for hitting 5-yr company targets of this form: 40\u201360%.\n   \u2022 New licensing category (Streaming/Cloud) reaching >$300M ARR: 25\u201335%.\n   \u2022 Large litigation-driven business model maintaining margins >50% for 5 yrs: ~50%.\n   \u2022 \"Platform transition\" success (handset \u2192 multi-segment): ~30%.\n\n1.5-2 Deviation from base rate:\n   My base case assumes 55% probability of hitting $1B ARR by 2030 \u2014 at the\n   high end of the base-rate range. Justification (3+ company-specific):\n   1) ARR already at $626M with 3 of 4 segments active; streaming just signed its\n      first agreement (Amazon) \u2014 early but demonstrated.\n   2) UPC injunctions against Disney (11 countries) show enforcement bite that\n      historically converts unlicensed usage into paid licenses.\n   3) The 2026 guidance raise (+$85M) and Q2'26 82% revenue beat vs. outlook show\n      execution credibility in converting litigation into contracts.\n   Justification is adequate; no further base-rate penalty.\n\n1.5-3 Base-rate shock check: Success probability (55%) is within 1.5x base (60%).\n   No red flag. ABSORBED.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 2 \u2014 BUSINESS QUALITY\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n2-1 Business understanding (3 sentences):\n   InterDigital invents wireless (2G\u21926G) and video (HEVC/AVC/AV1-family) technology\n   and licenses its patents to smartphone OEMs, CE/IoT/automotive makers, and now\n   streaming/cloud services. Revenue is annuity-like (ARR $626M) plus lumpy catch-up\n   payments from newly signed or renegotiated contracts. It is a patent tollbooth\n   funded by $211M/yr R&D, with gross margins ~97% and a net-cash balance sheet.\n   Understandability: HIGH.\n\n2-2 Moat score:\n   Intangible assets (patents/standards): 3\n   Switching costs: 1 (implementers must license, but FRAND caps pricing)\n   Network effects: 2 (standards adoption compounds portfolio value)\n   Cost advantage: 0\n   Economies of scale: 3 (R&D scale vs. licensees)\n   Regulatory barriers: 2 (SEP/FRAND regime + injunctive relief)\n   Data moat: 1 (patent citation/claim data)\n   TOTAL: 12/21 \u2192 WIDE MOAT (11\u201315).\n   Moat direction: STABLE\u2192WIDENING (streaming licensing established, 6G R&D\n   pipeline, AI-video patents; partially offset by antitrust scrutiny).\n\n2-3 Lynch classification: FAST GROWER with cyclical/litigation lumps.\n   Core checkpoints: ARR growth (13% \u2014 pass); earnings quality (accruals \u22120.07 \u2014\n   pass); balance sheet (net cash \u2014 pass); lumpiness (catch-up swings \u2014 manage).\n\n2-4 Financial strength scorecard:\n   Revenue CAGR (5-yr): +18.4% [Arithmetic, pack]\n   TTM revenue: $0.788B [Actual]\n   Operating margin TTM: 55.3% [Arithmetic] | 12-yr median 40.5%\n   Net margin: 38\u201345% [Actual/Arithmetic]\n   ROE: 26.4% [Aggregator] | ROIC: see Layer 2.5\n   FCF: $555M TTM [Arithmetic]; FY25 FCF $529M (filed P/E capex basis) [Arithmetic]\n   FCF conversion: OCF 544 / NI 407 = 1.34x FY25 [Arithmetic]\n   Net debt: NET CASH $829M [Estimate \u2014 see Section 3 debt treatment]\n   Judgment: EXCELLENT.\n\n2-5 Capital allocation scorecard (0\u20133 each):\n   1) Buyback efficiency: 1 (Q2'26 bought back $23M only; FY25 net share issuance\n      +16.0% due to converts/SBC \u2014 dilution is the dominant effect)\n   2) M&A track record: 2 (no dilutive acquisitions; disciplined)\n   3) Capex efficiency: 3 (incremental ROIC on R&D >40%; asset-light)\n   4) Mix rationality: 3 (R&D + modest buyback + dividend)\n   5) Guidance accuracy: 3 (Q2'26 beat guidance by 82%; repeated raises)\n   Insider bonus: 0 (insider ownership 1.58%; no cluster-buy data [Unconfirmed])\n   TOTAL: 12/15.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 2.5 \u2014 INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n2.5-1 R&D capitalization:\n   R&D: 2025 $211.4M; 2024 $196.9M; 2023 $195.3M [Actual, 10-K/proxy]\n   2022 est. $180M [Estimate]. 4-yr straight-line amortization (\u00a72025) \u2248 $196M.\n   Adjusted EBIT = $461M + $211M \u2212 $196M = $476M [Estimate].\n2.5-2 SBC: FY25 $43M [Actual]. Adjusted FCF = $529M \u2212 $43M = $486M [Estimate].\n2.5-3 Operating leases $18M added to debt [Actual].\n2.5-4 Brand/data: N/A for licensing; patents ARE the asset (covered in R&D capitalization).\n2.5-5 Adjusted ROIC:\n   Adjusted NOPAT = $476M \u00d7 0.86 \u2248 $409M [Estimate]\n   Adjusted invested capital = equity $1,101M + debt (LT $16M + converts $380M +\n   leases $18M) + unamortized R&D est. $644M \u2212 cash+investments $1,243M = $916M [Estimate]\n   Adjusted ROIC \u2248 45% vs. GAAP ROE 26%. Gap >5pp explained by R&D expensing.\n2.5-6 Owner earnings (Buffett): NI $407M + D&A $78M + R&D amortization $196M \u2212\n   R&D expense $211M \u2212 maintenance capex $20M \u2212 \u0394WC (catch-up timing, \u22480) =\n   ~$450M FY25 [Estimate]; normalized ~$380\u2013420M.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3 \u2014 VALUATION (ENGINE SELECTION + APPLICATION)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 0-1 Archetype: This is NOT a clean \"Software-Application\" name. The annuity\n   ARR base ($626M) makes it partially a Quality Compounder (B), but future value is\n   dominated by streaming/IoT/6G/AI optionality \u2192 Option-Led (E) overlay.\n   TRANSITION STATUS: Option-Led \u2192 Quality Compounder; >80% criteria met\n   (ARR/revenue >50%, GM >97%, FCF+ >2 quarters). Apply:\n   Blended engine = 70% Engine 1 (traditional DCF) + 30% Engine 4 (expectation/reverse DCF).\n   Transition conviction \u22120.5.\n\nEngine 1: DCF (Base Case)\nDiscount-rate derivation:\n   Rf = 4.74% [Actual, FRED 2026-08-21]\n   ERP = 4.5% [Assumption]\n   Beta = 1.20 [Assumption \u2014 vendor 1.412 is window-undisclosed; 1.2 reflects\n          net-cash balance sheet offsetting licensing cyclicality]\n   CoE = 4.74 + 1.2\u00d74.5 = 10.14% [Arithmetic]\n   After-tax CoD = 4.5%\u00d7(1\u22120.14) = 3.87% [Estimate \u2014 3.5% coupon converts]\n   Weights: 5% debt / 95% equity (actual net-cash structure) [Estimate]\n   WACC = 9.82% \u2192 rounded 9.75% [Estimate]\n\nForecast drivers (each sourced):\n   Revenue: 2026 at guidance midpoint $810M [Actual guidance];\n   2027\u20132030 path derived from management ARR target: ARR $626M (Q2'26) \u2192 $1B by 2030\n   = ~10.5% ARR CAGR, plus catch-up fading from ~$184M to ~$80M. Forecast:\n   2027 $875M (+8%), 2028 $950M (+8.6%), 2029 $1,030M (+8.4%), 2030 $1,100M (+6.8%).\n   [This exact path is an [Assumption] anchored to the $1B ARR target; the target\n   itself is [Actual] management guidance. After 2030 the path is NOT established;\n   terminal growth 3% assumes ARR maturation, not acceleration.]\n   EBIT margin: 2026 46% (enforcement costs elevated: Q2 opex +$25.8M; guided NI\n   implies ~45% GAAP EBIT margin) [Estimate]; 2027 50%; 2028-29 52%; 2030 53%\n   (normalizing legal costs, streaming scale) [Assumption].\n   D&A: $78M FY25, growing ~3%/yr [Estimate, from filed D&A].\n   SBC: $43M FY25, growing 5%/yr [Estimate, from filed SBC].\n   Capex: $70M/yr \u2014 filed P/E capex $16M + capitalized software/production assets\n   $54M [Estimate reconciling pack's filed vs vendor 4.44x discrepancy; the pack\n   explicitly says the filed FCF is overstated vs. broader definition].\n   Tax: 14% effective [Estimate \u2014 FY25 NI/EBIT implies ~12%; add 2pp for mix].\n   \u0394WC: 0 (catch-up timing swings are mean-reverting) [Assumption].\n\nDCF TABLE (base, $M) [Estimate \u2014 all rows]\n   Year   Rev    EBIT%  EBIT   NOPAT  +D&A  \u2212SBC  \u2212Capex  FCF   DF@p   PV\n   2026   810    46%    373    320    80    45    72     283   0.955  270\n   2027   875    50%    438    376    83    47    74     338   0.870  294\n   2028   950    52%    494    425    85    49    76     385   0.793  305\n   2029   1,030  52%    536    461    88    51    79     419   0.723  303\n   2030   1,100  53%    583    501    90    54    81     456   0.659  300\n   Sum PV FCF = 1,472\n   Terminal value = 456\u00d71.03/(0.0975\u22120.03) = 6,956\n   PV of TV = 4,584\n   EV = 6,056\n   Net cash: cash $739M + ST i