C \u2248 11.0% (net cash means no debt-weight drag; method note:\n    we discount unlevered FCF at 11% and add net cash at par;\n    interest income on cash is thus capitalized at par, a\n    conservative treatment)\n\nExplicit forecast (all $M) \u2014 every driver sourced below the table:\n| Fiscal | Recurring | Catch-up | Total | EBITDA | D&A | EBIT | NOPAT | Capex | \u0394WC | Unlvd FCF |\n|--------|-----------|----------|-------|--------|-----|------|-------|-------|-----|-----------|\n| 2026E  | 620       | 190      | 810   | 499    | 78  | 421  | 387   | 20    | 20  | 425       |\n| 2027E  | 720       | 120      | 840   | 521    | 80  | 441  | 406   | 20    | 20  | 446       |\n| 2028E  | 800       | 100      | 900   | 558    | 80  | 478  | 440   | 20    | 20  | 480       |\n| 2029E  | 885       | 90       | 975   | 605    | 80  | 525  | 483   | 20    | 20  | 523       |\n| 2030E  | 975       | 75       | 1,050 | 651    | 80  | 571  | 525   | 20    | 20  | 565       |\n| 2031E  | 1,050     | 50       | 1,100 | 682    | 80  | 602  | 554   | 20    | 10  | 604       |\n| 2032E  | 1,100     | 45       | 1,145 | 698    | 80  | 618  | 569   | 20    | 10  | 619       |\n| 2033E  | 1,144     | 40       | 1,184 | 710    | 80  | 630  | 580   | 20    | 10  | 630       |\n| 2034E  | 1,180     | 35       | 1,215 | 729    | 80  | 649  | 597   | 20    | 10  | 647       |\n\nSOURCE DISCIPLINE \u2014 every driver:\n  \u2022 Recurring revenue path: anchored to Q2 2026 exit ARR $625.7M\n    [Actual: press release] and the management target of $1B ARR\n    by 2030 [Actual: management target via research brief,\n    SeekingAlpha secondary \u2014 treat as [Actual: company statement]).\n    Interpolation 2026\u20132030 = ~12% CAGR [Assumption]. Post-2030\n    fade 8%\u21923% [Assumption]. BEYOND 2027 THERE IS NO COMPANY\n    GUIDANCE; the post-2027 path is my assumption and is stress-\n    tested in the tornado below.\n  \u2022 Catch-up: derived from FY2026 guide (total 810 \u2212 recurring\n    620 \u2248 190, consistent with H1 actual catch-up $167.3M [Actual\n    arithmetic]) and my assumption that the portfolio becomes\n    progressively licensed. Catch-up >25% of revenue into 2027\n    would signal earnings-quality deterioration versus this path.\n  \u2022 EBITDA margin: 61.6% in 2026E = guidance midpoint $499M /\n    $810M [Actual arithmetic]; 62% through 2031 = FY2025 actual\n    64.6% [Arithmetic] less conservatism for revenue-share costs\n    (LG TV deal) [Assumption]; 60\u201361% in the fade [Assumption].\n  \u2022 D&A: $78M FY2025 [Actual], held flat. Amortization of\n    acquired intangibles may decline eventually; no data to model\n    a decline [Assumption].\n  \u2022 Capex: $20M [Estimate]. Filed PPE capex FY2025 = $16M;\n    vendor = $71M (likely includes capitalized software). The\n    pack flags a 4.44\u00d7 disagreement. I use $20M acknowledging\n    the true number may be higher; the model is insensitive\n    (\u00b1$50M capex \u2248 \u00b1$1.50/share).\n  \u2022 \u0394WC: \u2212$20M initial, \u2212$10M later [Assumption]. History is\n    violently lumpy (\u2212$787M to +$219M); the small figure reflects\n    a steady-state portfolio with no major new-signing surges.\n  \u2022 Tax: 8% effective [Estimate]. Implied by 2026 guidance:\n    non-GAAP EPS $11.83 \u00d7 34.5M diluted \u2248 $408M vs EBITDA 499 \u2212\n    D&A 78 \u2248 421 \u2192 implied tax ~6\u20138%. FDII + R&D credits.\n  \u2022 Terminal growth: 2.5% [Assumption], below long-run nominal\n    GDP (~3.5\u20134%).\n\nDCF \u2014 unlevered FCF discounted at 11.0% (end-year convention):\n  PV 2026\u20132034 = $2,922M\n  Terminal value 2034 = 647 \u00d7 1.025 / (0.11 \u2212 0.025) = $7,802M\n  PV of TV = $3,050M\n  Operating value = $5,972M\n  + Net cash (cash 739 + ST inv 504 \u2212 total debt 488) = +$755M\n  = Equity value = $6,727M\n  \u00f7 34.5M diluted shares [Actual: 34.474M FY2025 wtd-avg]\n  \u2192 INTRINSIC VALUE = $195 per share (rounded)\n\nMultiples cross-check (must not rely on DCF alone):\n  \u2022 2026E non-GAAP EPS $11.83 [Actual guidance midpoint]:\n    fair P/E 16\u201322\u00d7 [Assumption for a quality-but-litigation-exposed\n    licensor] \u2192 $190\u2013260. At $342 the stock trades at 29\u00d7 non-GAAP.\n  \u2022 EV/EBITDA: EV = 11,813 \u2212 755 = 11,058 / 499 = 22.2\u00d7 2026E\n    [Arithmetic]. Quality compounders with legal overhangs\n    typically trade 12\u201318\u00d7. [Assumption]\n  \u2022 Reverse-DCF (Engine 4): the market's $342 price implies either\n    (a) ARR reaching $1.5B+ by 2030 and 3% terminal growth at a\n    9% discount rate, or (b) sustaining >25\u00d7 non-GAAP EPS into\n    perpetuity. Both are excessive relative to the 20\u201330% base\n    rate of platform-transition success.\n\nTornado sensitivity (top-3 variables, \u00b11\u03c3):\n  1. Discount rate (10%\u201312%): IV $240 \u2192 $165 (dominant)\n  2. 2030 ARR ($850M\u2013$1.2B): IV $172 \u2192 $230\n  3. EBITDA margin (58%\u201365%): IV $180 \u2192 $210\n  \u2192 These three variables become the thesis KPIs.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u2022 Competitive response: if IDCC successfully extracts large\n  streaming royalties, major licensors (Nokia, Ericsson,\n  Qualcomm) may push their own streaming programs; streamers may\n  unite behind antitrust challenges (Disney already has).\n  Net second-order drag: \u22122.\n\u2022 Reflexivity: positive \u2014 high royalty wins and a rising stock\n  attract R&D talent (SBC $43M/yr) and validate the licensing\n  model in new industries. Negative \u2014 an adverse DOJ/antitrust\n  outcome would trigger a de-rating that feeds back into weaker\n  negotiating leverage with unlicensed firms. Asymmetry is mild\n  negative at T0.\n\u2022 Customer behavior evolution: smartphone market is saturated;\n  growth now comes from streaming/cloud (Amazon Prime Video,\n  Disney+) and IoT/auto. LTV is high (license renews with every\n  device generation) and churn is structurally ~0 \u2014 you cannot\n  stop using a standard. The main evolution risk is political/\n  regulatory (FRAND rate-capping), not commercial.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 4. SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nPriors: Framework base rate for platform-transition success\n20\u201330%; my company-adjusted prior 50%.\n\nScenario table (probabilities sum to 100%):\n  \u2022 BEAR (30%): DOJ/Disney antitrust theory prevails; FRAND caps\n    bind; ARR stalls ~$750M by 2030; streaming fails to scale;\n    catch-up collapses to zero by 2029; margins 55%; discount 12%.\n    IV \u2248 $120. 50% CI low anchor.\n  \u2022 BASE (50%): ARR hits $1B by 2030; streaming partial success;\n    margins 62%; discount 11%; catch-up decays to ~3% of revenue.\n    IV \u2248 $195.\n  \u2022 BULL (20%): ARR reaches $1.2B by 2030; Amazon arbitration\n    awards high streaming rates; Disney settles; margins 64%;\n    discount 10%; catch-up persists at ~8% of revenue. IV \u2248 $290.\n\nBayesian note: the Q2 2026 revenue beat (+82% vs guidance) raises\nthe licensing execution likelihood substantially; however, that\nsame beat was almost entirely catch-up (Amazon $103.7M) \u2014 a\none-time deferral event, not a recurring uplift. I therefore\nupdate the prior only from 40% to 50% for the base case.\n\nExpected intrinsic value = 0.30\u00d7120 + 0.50\u00d7195 + 0.20\u00d7290 = $192\n\u2248 $190. 50% CI: $150\u2013240. 80% CI: $110\u2013290.\n\nMargin of safety: (190 \u2212 342.42)/190 = \u221280% \u2192 NONE.\nEven at the bull IV of $290, MoS = \u221218% \u2192 NONE.\nPrice embodies the bull case at best, and the base case is 44%\nbelow the current price.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 4.5. TIME HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nMarket-implied horizon: at 29\u00d7 2026E non-GAAP EPS with 13% ARR\ngrowth, the market is capitalizing roughly 7\u20139 years of flawless\nexecution (2033\u20132035 expectations).\nMy investment horizon: 3 years (2026\u20132029).\nSpread: ~4\u20135 years. A genuine arbitrage exists STRUCTURALLY, but\nin the WRONG DIRECTION for a buyer: the market has pulled forward\ntoo much value. The correction path could be (a) price falls\ntoward $200\u2013250, or (b) time passes and earnings grow into the\nprice (2029 diluted GAAP EPS \u2248 $15 \u2192 23\u00d7 would justify ~$345).\nPath (b) requires the multiple to stay rich. The expected route\nis a multi-year de-rating: over 3 years I see \u221220% to \u221235%\ntotal return.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 5. CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nConviction score (/15):\n  1. Business quality: 4/5 (wide moat, excellent financials)\n  2. Valuation attractiveness: 1/5 (price 80% above fair value)\n  3. Macro alignment: 2/5 (hawkish Fed vs long-duration asset)\n  4. Thesis clarity: 3/5 (KPIs clear: ARR, catch-up ratio,\n     arbitration outcomes)\n  5. Execution traceability: 3/5 (good disclosure; segment detail\n     absent; fee-based capex ambiguity)\n  TOTAL: 13/15 \u2014 but this score must be read as conviction IN THE\n  OVERVALUATION THESIS. Decision: HIGH conviction that IDCC at\n  $342 is unattractive.\n\nConviction decay: \u22121 point per 6 months absent confirming\nevidence; the valuation case only strengthens as time passes\nwithout catalysts, because the market must grow into the price.\n\nSizing: LONG = 0% (negative expected return). If held, reduce to\n\u22641% portfolio weight. Do not initiate a short at $342: 12.88%\nshort interest, 7.24 days-to-cover, rising M/M [Actual:\nAggregator] makes this a squeeze-prone crowded trade. The stock\ncan plausibly trade to $400\u2013450 on a favorable Amazon arbitration\nbefore converging to fair value.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 5.5. BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\u2022 Short interest: 12.88% of float, 2.74M shares, 7.24 DTC, +2.0\n  M/M [Actual: Aggregator, 2026-08-10, stale]. Elevated and\n  rising \u2192 contrarian squeeze risk; also signals that informed\n  capital is skeptical of the licensing model's durability.\n\u2022 Institutional ownership: vendor states 1.1% \u2014 almost certainly\n  a data error [Unconfirmed]. IDCC is an S&P MidCap 400 member\n  [Actual: Q1 2026 release]; institutional ownership is likely\n  80\u201395%. Any ETF-flow/rebalance dynamics flow WITH the market.\n\u2022 Insider activity: no cluster buying; management holds 1.58%\n  [Actual: Aggregator]. None of the \"insider buys\" signal.\n\u2022 Options positioning: no put/call skew data [Unconfirmed].\n\u2022 Sentiment: sell-side mean PT $462.67, high $488, low $425\n  [Actual: Aggregator, stale 2026-08-10]. Sell-side is 35% above\n  market \u2014 likely built on BASIC share count (462 \u00d7 25.8M =\n  $11.9B \u2248 342 \u00d7 34.5M = $11.8B). The analysts and the market\n  are pricing the same dollar equity value; the PER-SHARE\n  confusion is the behavioral crux.\n\u2022 Crowding risk score: 12/15 (high). Hedge-fund crowding on the\n  SHORT side + index holding on the long side = elevated two-way\n  positioning risk. Position-size reduction: \u22121%p on any long.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 6. PORTFOLIO FIT\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nIDCC is a high-beta (1.41 [Aggregator]), long-duration, rate-\nsensitive, litigation-exposed equity. It behaves like a\ndisguised-growth/optionality asset with quality cash flows.\nPortfolio role: it would fit only in the \"quality compounder\"\nbucket, but fails the valuation gate. Better substitutes at T0:\n(1) net-cash compounders with no antitrust overhang; (2) index\nbonds at 4.7% with zero binary legal risk. Within a diversified\nbook, IDCC adds tail-risk correlation to (a) a rates selloff,\n(b) a regulatory crackdown on IP/tech, and (c) a risk-off\nde-rating of long-duration assets. Its diversifying value is low.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 6.5. KELLY SIZING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nLong Kelly: edge = (IV \u2212 P)/P = (190 \u2212 342)/342 = \u221244% \u2192 0% long.\nFor a SHORT (not recommended): expected return \u2248 probability of\nconvergence (~55% over 3yr) \u00d7 (342\u2212190)/342 \u2248 +24%, but the\nvariance is extreme (squeeze to $450+ has ~15\u201320% probability).\nFull-Kelly short \u2248 5\u20137%; half-Kelly \u2248 3%. I do NOT recommend the\nshort due to binary legal catalysts (Amazon arbitration could\nlegitimately add $80\u2013150M ARR, pushing the stock through $400).\nBut note the framework's Layer 5 vs 6.5 gap: if a 3% short\nposition is held, it must be paired with a stop above $412.60\n(the 52-week high) and position cap of 3%.\n\nFinal sizing decision: 0% long, 0% short. If benchmark-constrained\nand forced to hold: \u22641% weight, with puts if available.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 7. RISKS & CATALYSTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nRisks to the intrinsic-value estimate (upside risks to price):\n  \u2022 Amazon binding arbitration award (due before mid-2027) could\n    set streaming royalties high \u2192 2027\u20132028 ARR upside of\n    $80\u2013150M [Unconfirmed outcome; catalyst].\n  \u2022 Disney litigation: IDCC already won two UPC injunctions across\n    11 countries [Actual: Q2 2026 release] \u2192 settlement at\n    favorable rates.\n  \u2022 DOJ/Disney antitrust outcome MAY be benign (\"urges caution\"\n    in Oct 2025 filing [Actual: DOJ PDF via ipwatchdog]).\n  \u2022 Persistent short interest \u2192 squeeze potential.\nRisks to the downside (downside price risks):\n  \u2022 DOJ antitrust theory accepted \u2192 royalty-rate caps or\n    injunction limits.\n  \u2022 Catch-up revenue normalization: FY2025\u2019s $529M FCF is not the\n    run-rate; if the market only now realizes this, de-rating.\n  \u2022 Diluted share count drift: 6.0M warrants (strike $105.43)\n    add ~4.1M shares at T0 prices; any additional issuance\n    pressures per-share value.\n  \u2022 10Y > 5% \u2192 IV down ~10% per 50bp of discount-rate rise.\n\nCatalysts in the next 12 months:\n  1. Amazon arbitration award (2027)\n  2. Disney settlement or adverse summary judgment\n  3. Q3\u2013Q4 2026 results vs raised guidance (Q3 guide $154\u2013158M)\n  4. Streaming/cloud ARR disclosure (first full-year run-rate)\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 7.5. CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nCommon bear triggers shared across a typical growth/momentum\nbook: rising 10Y, tightening Fed, USD strength, risk-off\nliquidity demand, tech/antitrust headlines.\n  \u2022 Conditional on a 1\u03c3 rate shock (+40bp 10Y): IDCC likely \u22128%\n    to \u221212% (beta 1.41 \u00d7 duration).\n  \u2022 Conditional on a \u221215% market shock (CVaR 95%): IDCC expected\n    \u2248 \u221222% to \u221227% [Estimate]; worse than the market due to\n    short-interest-driven amplification.\n  \u2022 Tail correlation with other high-multiple tech: HIGH (>0.8\n    in 2022-style regime [Estimate]). A portfolio already\n    long growth should NOT add IDCC; a portfolio long value/\n    cyclicals gets diversification benefit but also idiosyncratic\n    legal risk. Net recommendation: 0%.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 8. MONITORING RULES\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nAutomated re-evaluation triggers (any ONE hit = full re-run):\n  KPI 1 \u2014 Streaming/Cloud + IoT ARR: if the combined non-\n    smartphone ARR does not exceed $150M by Q4 2027, reduce bull\n    probability and revalue down.\n  KPI 2 \u2014 Total ARR growth <5% YoY for two consecutive quarters:\n    base case downgraded; IV \u221220%.\n  KPI 3 \u2014 Catch-up revenue >25% of total revenue in FY2027:\n    earnings-quality flag; IV \u221210%.\n  KPI 4 \u2014 Diluted share count >36.0M: IV \u22125% per 1M extra shares.\n  KPI 5 \u2014 DOJ/Disney adverse ruling (summary judgment against\n    IDCC on Sherman Act claims): IV \u221225% to \u221230% immediately.\n  KPI 6 \u2014 Amazon arbitration streaming run-rate <$80M/yr: the\n    streaming/cloud option layer fails; IV \u221210%.\n  KPI 7 \u2014 10Y yield >5.0%: discount rate +0.5%; IV \u221210%.\n\nBuy-back (re-entry) trigger: price \u2264 $230 with ARR still growing\n>10% and no adverse legal ruling \u2192 MoS becomes positive (~20%);\nat \u2264 $200 \u2192 strong buy zone.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 9. RED TEAM (ADVERSARIAL)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 9-1. Short/bear thesis (5\u20137 bullets, using the same data):\n  1. True fully-diluted market cap is $11.8B, not the headline\n     $8.8B; the 25.8M basic share count misleads retail.\n  2. 2026 guidance implies GAAP EPS \u2248 $10\u201310.5 diluted \u2192 33\u00d7 P/E;\n     non-GAAP 29\u00d7; EV/EBITDA 22\u00d7 on a business whose catch-up\n     revenue (\u224825% of 2026E) is non-recurring by definition.\n  3. FY2025 FCF of $529M was inflated by catch-up collections;\n     normalized owner earnings are $400\u2013430M, making the \"cheap\n     FCF\" narrative an artifact.\n  4. The DOJ Statement of Interest in Disney v. InterDigital\n     legitimizes an antitrust attack on SEP licensing practices;\n     an adverse final ruling could cap royalty rates across the\n     entire portfolio [Unconfirmed outcome].\n  5. ARR growth of 13% is decelerating from the 2023\u20132025\n     catch-up-driven surge; the $1B-ARR-by-2030 target requires a\n     new industry (streaming) to scale within 4 years \u2014 a 20\u201330%\n     base-rate event.\n  6. 6.0M warrants (strike $105.43) plus conversion excess on\n     $380M of notes will mechanically add ~7\u20138M shares by\n     mid-2028; holders of basic-share-count P/E are buying a\n     hidden 33% dilution.\n  7. The 52-week range ($249\u2013413) already shows the stock round-\n     tripped once; a repeat of 2022-style de-rating is plausible.\n\nStep 9-2. Logic combat score:\n  Long-side logic: 5.5/10 (quality, ARR momentum, squeeze fuel are\n  real; but valuation ignores dilution and catch-up).\n  Short/avoid-side logic: 7.0/10 (valuation rigor, dilution\n  disclosure, base-rate discipline). Gap = 1.5 < 2 \u2192 NO conviction\n  downgrade needed, but the gap is uncomfortably close; monitor\n  for squeeze-driven price action that would make the short\n  unattractive (already the case \u2192 we do NOT short).\n\nStep 9-3. Adversarial data: no Hindenburg-style report exists\n[Unconfirmed]; the principal adversarial inputs are the DOJ\nStatement of Interest [Actual] and the Disney antitrust complaint\n[Actual: Aug 2025 per research brief]. Both are public-record and\nare incorporated.\n\nStep 9-4. Killed arguments:\n  \u2022 \"The market cap is only $8.8B / 17\u00d7 FCF\" \u2014 KILLED by the\n    diluted share count. Revives only if the company repurchases\n    or retires the warrants below intrinsic value (unlikely at\n    $342).\n  \u2022 \"Injunctions against Disney prove pricing power\" \u2014 KILLED as\n    a standalone bull point; injunctions also provoke antitrust\n    escalation. Revives if Disney settles at high rates AND the\n    DOJ case is dismissed.\n  \u2022 \"Q2 2026 EPS crushed by 372%\" \u2014 KILLED as run-rate evidence;\n    it was mostly $103.7M of Amazon catch-up. Revives if ARR\n    ex-catch-up sustains >15% growth for 3+ quarters.\n  \u2022 \"Sell-side PT $462\" \u2014 KILLED as valuation evidence; it is\n    consistent with a basic-share-count mistake. Revives if\n    sell-side models convert to diluted counts and STILL target\n    >$400.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u250